.TH "SOMME" "1" "2026\-08\-08" "Somme 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
somme \- shared authenticated command\-line foundation for Somme
applications
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[CR]somme [\-a|\-\-app APP] [\-e|\-\-env\-prefix PREFIX] [\-u|\-\-api\-base URL] COMMAND\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Somme provides account\-profile persistence, bearer\-authenticated JSON
requests, rate\-limit reporting, and installable manuals for derived
product CLIs.
Product\-specific commands belong in derived clients such as Suffix and
Bay.
Secrets are stored in the platform configuration directory and are never
printed by configuration commands.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
\f[CR]\-a, \-\-app APP\f[R]
Configuration namespace.
Default: \f[CR]somme\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]\-e, \-\-env\-prefix PREFIX\f[R]
Prefix used for \f[CR]PREFIX_API_KEY\f[R] and
\f[CR]PREFIX_API_BASE\f[R].
Default: \f[CR]SOMME\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]\-u, \-\-api\-base URL\f[R]
Default API base for newly saved accounts.
.TP
\f[CR]\-h, \-\-help\f[R]
Print help.
.TP
\f[CR]\-V, \-\-version\f[R]
Print the version.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS login
\f[CR]somme login [\-t|\-\-token TOKEN] [\-u|\-\-api\-base URL] [\-a|\-\-account NAME] [\-e|\-\-email EMAIL] [\-r|\-\-tier TIER]\f[R]
.PP
Save a token and select its profile.
Without \f[CR]\-\-token\f[R], select an already\-authenticated saved
account.
\f[CR]\-\-account\f[R] defaults to the email, active account, or
\f[CR]default\f[R].
\f[CR]\-\-api\-base\f[R] overrides the product default.
\f[CR]\-\-email\f[R] and \f[CR]\-\-tier\f[R] cache non\-secret account
metadata.
.SS logout
\f[CR]somme logout [\-a|\-\-account NAME]\f[R]
.PP
Remove the selected account\(cqs token while preserving its profile.
.SS account
\f[CR]somme account [ls|use NAME]\f[R]
.PP
List saved profiles or select one.
The active profile is marked with \f[CR]*\f[R].
.SS config
\f[CR]somme config\f[R]
.PP
Print the namespace, active account, configuration path, and count of
stored tokens without printing secrets.
.SS request
\f[CR]somme request PATH [\-j|\-\-json]\f[R]
.PP
Send an authenticated GET request to \f[CR]PATH\f[R].
The compact JSON response goes to standard output; \f[CR]\-\-json\f[R]
pretty\-prints it.
Finite quota information is printed to standard error.
HTTP 429 failures include the reset epoch when supplied by the server.
.SS man
\f[CR]somme man [show]\f[R]
.PP
Print the complete embedded section\-1 manual.
.PP
\f[CR]somme man install [\-d|\-\-dir DIR]\f[R]
.PP
Install \f[CR]somme.1\f[R].
Without \f[CR]\-\-dir\f[R], Somme tries standard Homebrew, local,
user\-local, and system man directories as appropriate for the platform.
.SH ACCOUNTS AND CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is \f[CR]somme/config.toml\f[R] below the
platform configuration directory unless \f[CR]\-\-app\f[R] changes the
namespace.
It contains an active profile and named account records with API base,
bearer token, optional email and tier, and update time.
Command\-line product options take precedence over saved defaults.
Environment credentials take precedence when a derived client uses
\f[CR]Product::environment_account\f[R].
.SH RATE LIMITS
Somme reads \f[CR]X\-RateLimit\-Limit\f[R],
\f[CR]X\-RateLimit\-Remaining\f[R], and \f[CR]X\-RateLimit\-Reset\f[R].
The literal value \f[CR]unlimited\f[R] identifies an administrator
bypass.
Enforcement is server\-side; clients cannot grant themselves
administrator status.
.SH EXAMPLES
Save and use a token:
.IP
.EX
somme login \-a work \-t somme_sk_example \-u https://api.example.test
somme request \-j /v1/profile
.EE
.PP
Switch profiles and install the manual:
.IP
.EX
somme account use work
somme man install \-d \(ti/.local/share/man/man1
man somme
.EE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\f[CR]PREFIX_API_KEY\f[R]
Bearer token when a derived client uses the configured environment
prefix.
.TP
\f[CR]PREFIX_API_BASE\f[R]
API base paired with the environment token.
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[CR]APP/config.toml\f[R]
Named account profiles under the platform configuration directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success.
Nonzero indicates invalid arguments, missing configuration,
authentication or HTTP failure, rate exhaustion, serialization failure,
or manual installation failure.
